1. demo creates a fresh real-session owner, binds null inspector and true sessions, guards page fetches/CLI commands/clock continuations and registers idempotent cleanup (demo.ts 68–93, 130–139, 180–185). It owns a TEST SECRET used by session readers. Page openRoom requests a session and reads the directory/membership; if no session is issued, Page transport uses signed reads (data.ts 87–106, 228–255). The gate does not record which branch actually served this run.
2. Page act reads the current native declaration, supplies retained definition bytes, shapes the declared fields and detached body, signs and submits through actual transport, then attempts a summary refresh (data.ts 732–769). Directory open-issue accepts an act and opens a lane row. Its `scope` ref is absent until an applied child result; a refused/conflict child result leaves it absent (directory.ts 121–148). Its create-lane send carries the seed and native creation metadata (731–748).
