Concrete fixture gap: demo's `known` array contains only register and destination (149,158). `pause(waiting=[])` drives effect/dispatch only on known plus explicit waiting scopes (111–128). task-data calls it with no argument (109), so that call does not explicitly drive the directory that emitted this create or the child lane that must answer/index. Native commits start dispatchers in waitUntil (object.ts 218–223), but no caller awaits those background starts. Dispatcher returns a counted number for only its own running pass; it does not constitute transitive child quiescence (outbox.ts 103–170). This gap existed before the session migration: the ownership diff wraps existing calls in leases but preserves scope selection.

Repair proposal supported by source: give this fixture a deterministic bounded creation-completion boundary. After the accepted directory act, derive the actual child seed/ref from the directory's immutable recorded send, explicitly drive the directory and child in the scheduler, and require the native child result/confirmed scope reference before listing. At minimum include the directory in known and pass the exact child in waiting; including only the directory is not a complete transitive guarantee. Preserve the original body/list/title assertions and original 5-second timeout, and replace the non-null lookup with an explicit meaningful missing-row assertion so a future failure states the unmet boundary. Keep authenticated Page reads unchanged. This is an existing scheduler contract repair proposal, not a demonstrated cause of d026 or a reason to waive the failed gate.

